From 653f131f9153be0e8769fb93763194f3448e6e5f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 13:13:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban pickup-stall: one alarm when a held machine's
 own default-placement cards wait and no other machine copies them

Problem (t_01a1d4f2f591d595, 2026-11-13): t_01a1d49d50e4c656, the PR #2168
land-lane owner, woke ready at 12:32Z. It was default placement (runs_on NULL)
and created on worker-6, which was on a hub-worker-core-rollout hold (drain
only). Every pool worker picks up `explicit`, and kanban_worker_node._skip_reason
skips default-placement cards there. So no machine claimed it for 14 min, and
#2173 waited in the lane behind it. The pickup-stall detector filed nothing,
because it watched only foreign cards pinned machine:<host>.

Why-chain:
1. No machine took the Board lease: only worker-6 was eligible, and it was held.
2. Default placement means "its creator", and explicit pickup keeps every other
   worker off the card.
3. The rollout hold stops claims but does not re-place the cards only that
   worker may run.
Root (not caught): the stall detector skipped default-placement cards whose
only eligible machine is held.

Fix (core half; the state half moves such cards when the rollout holds a worker):
- kanban_pickup_stall_held.sweep runs on every dispatcher sweep of a held
  machine M. It looks for cards on M's board that are ready, unclaimed, default
  placement, created on M and use a scratch workspace, and that no other
  active, unheld, non-explicit pickup machine would copy (kanban_worker_node.
  eligible). If any has waited longer than kanban.sync.pickup_stall_seconds
  (600 s by default) since both its ready_since and the hold's start, it files
  ONE host-wide agent-owned alarm, keyed pickup-stall:<M>:held-default:. The
  alarm lists every such card and is placed off M (alarm_placement). Cards
  that a respawn guard holds are not listed.
- kanban_pickup_stall_repin: the alarm's re-place scope accepts a listed card
  that is still default placement and created on M (held_default_howto names
  the operator move to pool:worker).
- _create/_tail take an optional howto, so this alarm's body names the right
  move.

Tests: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_pickup_stall_held.py
- T1 core half: the rollout's exact `move <id> --pool --reason "<w> on rollout
  hold"` sets runs_on [pool:worker] and writes a moved event, and
  worker-1's explicit pickup, which skipped the card before, then copies it.
- T3: one alarm after the threshold, reused on the next sweep and placed on
  worker-1. Nothing is filed under the threshold, when another machine can
  claim the card, after the hold ends, after the move, or for a
  dir-workspace card.
RED on base: the T3 alarm test fails. GREEN: 5/5. The neighbouring suites
(pickup_held_budget/copy, pickup_stall, _repin, _reservation, worker_node) pass:
217 passed.
